(setter_cal -- tie the setter to the current workpiece)
(Run once per setup, after Z has been zeroed on the workpiece top with)
(whatever tool is in the collet:  o<setter_cal> call)
(Rerun after moving the setter, after a new workpiece, or after re-zeroing)
(Z by hand.)

(D is the setter trigger height in the active work coordinate system. It is a)
(property of the setup, not of the tool, so any later tool can be zeroed from)
(it. It is parked in the G59.3 origin, which this machine does not otherwise)
(use, because that parameter is persistent across restarts:)
(  #5383 = D, #5381 = 1 marks it valid. D is negative when the workpiece top)
(  sits above the setter trigger height, so a zero test will not do.)

o<setter_cal> sub

  M70

  o<setter_probe> call

  G10 L2 P9 X1 Z#5063

  (debug, setter calibrated: D = #5383 mm above work Z zero)

  G53 G0 Z#<_ini[TOOLSENSOR]SAFE_Z>

  M72

o<setter_cal> endsub
